WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:02.534
Hey Youtubers, it's Charlie.

00:00:02.534 --> 00:00:05.954
So tonight is the first night of Comic Con, they're screening the Supergirl pilot

00:00:05.954 --> 00:00:09.967
so I thought it was time to do my non-spoilery review.  Most of you probably won't be able to

00:00:09.967 --> 00:00:15.116
see it 'till the Fall so I'll do another review with Easter eggs and spoilers whenever that airs.

00:00:15.116 --> 00:00:19.796
For those that are wondering - they actually moved up the premiere date, so officially the series is

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:21.800
gonna start at the end of October.

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:27.340
It's a Monday night show at 8pm, so it's on at like the same Flash and Arrow are during the night.

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:30.374
So it'll be like: Monday is Supergirl, Tuesday is The Flash,

00:00:30.374 --> 00:00:35.361
and then Wednesday is Arrow. You could also consider the other DC shows kinda part of that universe.

00:00:35.361 --> 00:00:37.904
Like, you know - Gotham also airs on Fox.

00:00:37.904 --> 00:00:40.344
Gotham's in there too, that's still a Monday night show

00:00:40.344 --> 00:00:44.620
but I try to treat the Berlanti shows as like their own seperate Arrow-verse.

00:00:44.629 --> 00:00:49.176
So just rewind in time just a little bit. If you guys remember, last year this exact same thing

00:00:49.176 --> 00:00:50.576
happened with The Flash.

00:00:50.576 --> 00:00:55.856
They aired it a little bit early, you know a bunch of people got a chance to see it really early in the year.

00:00:55.900 --> 00:00:59.500
That can be bad sometimes, especially when there's a lot of marketing behind something.

00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:01.820
Just because you don't have any context for what you're seeing.

00:01:01.829 --> 00:01:04.689
Like you don't understand what their intent is - you just have to figure it out yourself.

00:01:04.689 --> 00:01:10.578
So a lot of times you can misinterpret certain things, which I feel like is happening with this Supergirl pilot.

00:01:10.578 --> 00:01:14.978
The fact that it's made by the same people that make The Flash should give you an idea for their intent.

00:01:14.980 --> 00:01:18.598
They're really trying to go with the same type of tone for that show.

00:01:18.598 --> 00:01:22.773
Even Arrow is swinging just a little bit lighter. I think they just had so much success with

00:01:22.773 --> 00:01:26.376
The Flash, with the way they wrote it - the way they concieved that, that they wanted to replicate

00:01:26.376 --> 00:01:28.637
that as much as possible with another character.

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:33.600
Some of you might point out that Supergirl is one of the angriest characters in the DC universe.

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:38.700
But that's not really the show that they're making, this is a show about a girl finding her place in the world.

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:42.620
Superman does exist, I mean don't plan on seeing him a whole lot, but it's like -

00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:46.400
you know, what do you do when the world already has a God-like figure?

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:49.240
It's like, it doesn't need you so what are you gonna do?

00:01:49.240 --> 00:01:55.131
I'm a big fan of the way The Flash uses humor, so I'm hoping that we get to see a lot of that on Supergirl too.

00:01:55.131 --> 00:02:00.040
Because, you have like a super-powered being so how could you not use those powers for comedy?

00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:02.640
It's harder to do that when she's pissed off all the time.

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:05.240
So, you get an idea of how it's much harder

00:02:05.240 --> 00:02:10.660
to build a series around an angry Supergirl than it is with just like a "normal" Supergirl.

00:02:10.660 --> 00:02:14.980
Typically what happens with pilots, though, is everyone's still trying to figure the characters out.

00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:17.580
Like, it took them all year on The Flash,

00:02:17.583 --> 00:02:21.960
even as different writers approached different characters, you know they all tried to find their voices

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:23.760
along with the actors themselves.

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:28.540
Like, Grant Gustin said that every single day on set he learned something new.

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:30.100
So you kinda look at the first season of any show

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:33.740
as a crash course in whatever group of characters they're dealing with.

00:02:33.740 --> 00:02:35.020
And for those that are asking, yes,

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:39.740
they will be able to do other Superman universe characters. People from those comics.

00:02:39.740 --> 00:02:43.960
But as you've seen from the trailers, the way they're surfacing a lot of those is through the Phantom Zone.

00:02:43.960 --> 00:02:46.840
That's where a lot of the threats are going to come from.

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:50.800
When everyone does have a chance to watch it I'll do a spoilery breakdown where I explain:

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:53.460
who these people are working for, who the villains are,

00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:57.920
and based on the way they treated The Flash characters, how everything might go down this season.

00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:04.240
Even though it's part of the Berlanti-verse, it's technically kind of off in a bubble on the outside of the Arrowverse.

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:06.300
It's like a pocket universe for now.

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:10.460
The problem is that even though the writers, the producers, everyone that works on the show

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:15.440
wants to cross over with Arrow and The Flash, the network executives at CBS have to okay it.

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:18.360
And they said, season 1 - probably not gonna do any crossovers.

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:22.020
But if you remember the way Arrow dealt with super powers a couple years ago,

00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:25.120
rewind to Arrow season 1. Super powers don't exist.

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:29.600
That was the Party-line from the producers. They were like, "Super powers don't exist in this universe."

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:33.020
Cut to season 2, we see Barry Allen. Boom. Super powers everywhere.

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:36.480
Season 3, we start to see some magic via the Lazarus Pit.

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:39.020
Season 4, we get to time travel.

00:03:39.020 --> 00:03:43.180
So even though they say season 1 of Supergirl - no crossovers with Arrow and The Flash..

00:03:43.180 --> 00:03:44.700
just wait 'till season 2.

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:49.200
And typically what happens in a season, especially a season with like 20+ episodes

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:51.480
is they'll do like 3 micro-arcs.

00:03:51.480 --> 00:03:55.660
Where they'll tell this self-contained story for like the first 8 episodes, like the first half of the season

00:03:55.660 --> 00:03:59.700
and then the second half, they'll have like a second small story arc when they come back from break

00:03:59.700 --> 00:04:02.080
and then finally, their big final act.

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:04.840
Like the whole season works as a 3-Act Play.

00:04:04.840 --> 00:04:09.420
So, the first half of the season is probably going to be her unlocking her abilities.

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:12.920
There's a good reason why she's just as powerful as Superman..

00:04:12.920 --> 00:04:16.180
but she just doesn't have the command of her abilities that he does.

00:04:16.180 --> 00:04:18.560
I can't really explain that in great detail without getting into spoilers,

00:04:18.560 --> 00:04:21.940
so I'll explain that the next time I do a Supergirl review.

00:04:21.940 --> 00:04:25.640
The other thing that really grabbed me about the pilot is the Jimmy Olsen character.

00:04:25.640 --> 00:04:27.980
They're very clearly setting him up to be a big deal.

00:04:27.980 --> 00:04:33.120
Like, one of the few characters that doesn't have any sinister motives or some side angle that he's trying to work.

00:04:33.220 --> 00:04:36.620
Just watching out for Kara on Superman's orders.

00:04:36.620 --> 00:04:40.940
Just to explain the timeline a little bit, they kind of explained it in the trailer, but basically:

00:04:40.940 --> 00:04:43.680
Jimmy Olsen is post-Superman at this point.

00:04:43.680 --> 00:04:47.780
Like, he's kind of come up through the ranks, made a name for himself at the Daily Planet..

00:04:47.780 --> 00:04:50.720
Superman asks him to go help Kara.

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:56.420
So for those wondering about where this exists in the timeline of Batman v Superman in the movies,

00:04:56.420 --> 00:05:00.060
just consider it completely seperate. Completely different characters.

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:04.440
For those really hoping for Justice League though,  I feel like Supergirl is one step closer to that.

00:05:04.440 --> 00:05:08.840
She could totally take his place inside like a full-blown TV Justice League.

00:05:08.840 --> 00:05:13.400
Legends of Tomorrow kind of is that already, but it's closer to Justice Society because, I mean,

00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:18.000
Vandal Savage - just a much bigger Justice Society villain than he was a Justice League villain.

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:21.560
One of the things I really think they need to work on though is the fight scenes.

00:05:21.560 --> 00:05:23.900
Like, it's really easy to do a fight scene with Oliver.

00:05:23.900 --> 00:05:29.091
He's a normal human, you know, he just does a bunch of Krav Maga. A bunch of spinning. He shoots people with arrows. Pretty simple.

00:05:29.091 --> 00:05:33.580
When we got to Barry they had to alter his fighting style just based on his powers.

00:05:33.580 --> 00:05:35.960
Like, he's not a great fighter yet, but he's super fast.

00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:39.200
So he uses his speed in creative ways to take down villains.

00:05:39.200 --> 00:05:41.780
So, that's really what I want to see from Supergirl.

00:05:41.780 --> 00:05:44.720
The temptation when you have like a super strong character

00:05:44.720 --> 00:05:50.600
is to just have them punch through walls, just do like - a lot of smashy stuff, and I don't think that that's that interesting.

00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:57.320
But you guys can let me know, I feel like they do have some really interesting opportunities to use her powers in creative ways when it comes to taking down villains.

00:05:57.340 --> 00:05:59.400
Or using her powers for humor.

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:02.704
The operating mantra is Humor, Heart, Spectacle.

00:06:02.704 --> 00:06:05.620
The Spectatle part is pretty easy to do when you have super powers.

00:06:05.620 --> 00:06:09.040
The heart is really where the supporting characters come in,

00:06:09.040 --> 00:06:13.180
so I feel like it's gonna take a few episodes for them to build that team around Kara

00:06:13.180 --> 00:06:15.640
before we get a feel for the moral core of the show.

00:06:15.640 --> 00:06:18.920
Her family life - not exactly like Barry's family life.

00:06:18.920 --> 00:06:22.940
She does not have like a Joe or Iris West to anchor herself to.

00:06:22.940 --> 00:06:28.940
They do explore her relationship with her Kryptonian family, and that's like a really important part of the pilot

00:06:28.940 --> 00:06:31.780
but it gets kind of spoilery so I'll just table that for now.

00:06:31.780 --> 00:06:37.600
But if you do want to talk about some of the twists with respect to her family, just please use Spoiler Tags.

00:06:37.600 --> 00:06:39.740
So really important dates to remember:

00:06:39.740 --> 00:06:46.180
October 26 - that Monday is the premiere of the first episode, but some of you will just be watching it again.

00:06:46.180 --> 00:06:49.700
What's probably gonna happen is, it'll probably run up to the beginning of December.

00:06:49.700 --> 00:06:53.820
Most shows go on break by the second week in December, if not the first week or before that.

00:06:53.820 --> 00:06:55.660
That's usually when Arrow and The Flash go on break.

00:06:55.660 --> 00:06:58.640
Then it'll come back around the same time Arrow and The Flash come back.

00:06:58.640 --> 00:07:00.797
That also when Legends of Tomorrow starts.

00:07:00.797 --> 00:07:05.717
They haven't announced when that's gonna premiere, but they're probably gonna do that during the big DC Super Panel.

00:07:05.717 --> 00:07:11.700
Just a heads-up on that, I'm gonna be backstage with the Arrow and Flash people, so I'm like, I'm super pumped up about that.

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:15.860
But they said that I'm not allowed to record the screen, but they will give me some B-rolls

00:07:15.860 --> 00:07:19.640
so hopefully I will get some footage from the panel, but it's gonna be a little weird.

00:07:19.640 --> 00:07:24.290
I will be live-tweeting though so if you want to follow me on Twitter and Facebook, there's links for that in the Description.

00:07:24.290 --> 00:07:27.280
The first panel that I'm gonna be uploading this week is gonna be tomorrow.

00:07:27.280 --> 00:07:29.360
That'll either be Dr. Who or Sherlock.

00:07:29.360 --> 00:07:33.340
So just check my Youtube homepage every once in awhile, or just check my Twitter feed.

00:07:33.340 --> 00:07:37.620
So while you guys wait for the rest of my Comic Con videos to start posting, I'm gonna add 'em to my Master List.

00:07:37.620 --> 00:07:41.820
You can click here to see all those videos. It's just like a special Comic Con playlist.

00:07:41.820 --> 00:07:45.400
And you can click here to learn what's going on with The Flash and Arrow at Comic Con.

00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:49.020
Thank you so much for watching! Everybody, let's high-five. I'll see you guys this weekend.

00:07:49.420 --> 00:07:55.900
(music playing)

